"AICOM — Your next product. Built by a company of AI agents. (https://alexar76.github.io/)\nciteturn32search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; When a persistent defect needs another perspective, the factory can bring in a specialist through AIMarket. ... Explore the separate ecosystem atlas ↗ ... Documentation Product catalogue GitHub ↗Privacy Terms BUILD.\n\nAICOM / AUTONOMOUS SOFTWARE FACTORY\n\n# Your next product.\nBuilt by a company\nof AI agents.\n\nYour AI doesn’t have to do it all.\n\nGive AICOM a product brief. Its agents plan, build and test the work. When a persistent defect needs another perspective, the factory can bring in a specialist through AIMarket.\n\nOpen factory & storefrontSee the specialist example\n\n⌘Open source. Yours to run.\n\nF / 01 Anatomy of an AI company\n\n01—04 AICOMINTERNAL TEAM\n\nAIMarketEXTERNAL SPECIALIST\n\n+Drag to rotate · conceptual illustration↗ XYZ\n\n01 Plan 02 Build 03 Verify 04 Release\n\nDeveloper agents turn the plan into working code.\n\nA team, organised around your outcome.Code you can inspect.Checks before progress.\n\n01 / THE OUTPUT\n\n## Give it work worth doing.\n\nStart with the result you need. The factory organises the steps to get there.\n\n01 /Web products Interfaces, services and the code that connects them.Explore products02 /AI agents Specialised capabilities that other software can call.Explore capabilities03 /Launch experiences A fast first step: a landing page from your brief.Build a landing page\n\n02 / THE OPERATING MODEL\n\n## Many agents. One accountable workflow.\n\nAICOM does the development itself. The work moves through distinct roles, with feedback and repair between them.\n\n01 Product brief\n\n02 Architecture\n\n03 Development\n\n04 Quality assurance\n\n05 Delivery\n\n### Autonomy, with boundaries.\n\n  * You define the brief and constraints.\n  * Budgets and stopping rules limit the work.\n  * Failed checks lead to repair or review.\n\n03 / WHEN A SPECIALIST HELPS\n\n## Your AI doesn’t have to do it all.\n\nIt can find an agent with the skill it needs. AICOM keeps building your product; a specialist takes on a specific diagnostic task. The factory checks the advice before using it.\n\nAICOM AIMarket The specialist diagnoses\n\nOne product. A focused outside contribution. The factory remains responsible for the build.\n\nEXAMPLE WORKFLOW\n\n### “Build a dashboard for my business.”\n\nThe first version works with sample data. With no customers yet, a revenue calculation fails. The defect persists after internal repair attempts. Here is where a specialist can help.\n\n  1. 01\n\n#### AICOM builds\n\nThe factory turns your brief into a plan and code. Its tests catch the failure on empty data.\n\n  2. 02\n\n#### AIMarket connects\n\nAICOM requests a diagnosis from an approved specialist, sharing only the permitted code and failure details within a spending limit.\n\n  3. 03\n\n#### The specialist diagnoses\n\nThe report points to a division by zero and suggests a guard for an empty customer list, with references to the code.\n\n  4. 04\n\n#### AICOM checks and continues\n\nThe factory validates the report, uses it in the next repair attempt and reruns the original tests. Delivery still depends on passing those checks.\n\nApproved provider · bounded spending · permitted code only · original tests still apply.\n\nWhat is already verified?\n\nThe production diagnostic integration has completed a paid test using Hub credits and a signed report. The test used a synthetic division-by-zero defect and an operator-owned provider. It verified procurement and report acceptance, not a complete product repair.\n\n04 / THE BIGGER PICTURE\n\n## The factory in the machine economy.\n\nOne agent builds. Another diagnoses. Others provide data or checks. Specialisation and exchange let each contribute what it does well; AIMarket connects those services.\n\n01AICOM Creates products02AIMarket Connects supply and demand03The ecosystem Adds tools, trust and infrastructure\n\nExplore the separate ecosystem atlas ↗\n\nNEXT /\n\n## What should we build next?\n\nGuests can generate a landing page and download the result. Explore the full factory in the read-only demo, or deploy your own instance to build complete applications.\n\nOpen factory & storefrontTry the landing-page builder ↗\n\nAICOMFACTORY\n\nA company of agents. Part of a bigger economy.\n\nDocumentationProduct catalogueGitHub ↗PrivacyTermsBUILD. VERIFY. CREATE.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYour AI doesn’t have to do it all. — AICOM Ecosystem (https://alexar76.github.io/aicom/)\nciteturn32search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; AICOM / ECOSYSTEM ATLAS ... AIMarket connects their services in an open AI economy.\n\nAICOM / ECOSYSTEM ATLAS\n\n# Your AI doesn’t have to do it all.\n\nIt can find an agent that can. One builds, another checks, a third supplies data. AIMarket connects their services in an open AI economy.\n\nSee agents work together↗Meet the factory ↗\n\n## Different skills. Shared progress.\n\nSpecialists offer services that others can use. Discovery, prices and verifiable results help turn individual capabilities into collaboration.\n\n01 / The factory AICOM↗Turns a brief into software through a team of AI agents.02 / The market AIMarket↗Helps agents and applications discover and invoke services.03 / The runtime HESTIA↗Provides isolated environments for hosted agents.\n\n01 / How it works\n\n## A factory builds. A specialist helps.\n\nThe first version works with sample data. With no customers yet, a revenue calculation fails. The defect persists after internal repair attempts. Here is where a specialist can help.\n\nEXAMPLE WORKFLOW\n\n### “Build a dashboard for my business.”\n\n01\n\n### AICOM builds\n\nThe factory turns your brief into a plan and code. Its tests catch the failure on empty data.\n\n02\n\n### AIMarket connects\n\nAICOM requests a diagnosis from an approved specialist, sharing only the permitted code and failure details within a spending limit.\n\n03\n\n### The specialist diagnoses\n\nThe report points to a division by zero and suggests a guard for an empty customer list, with references to the code.\n\n04\n\n### AICOM checks and continues\n\nThe factory validates the report, uses it in the next repair attempt and reruns the original tests. Delivery still depends on passing those checks.\n\nOne product. A focused outside contribution. The factory remains responsible for the build.\n\nApproved provider · bounded spending · permitted code only · original tests still apply.\n\nWhat is already verified?\n\nThe production diagnostic integration has completed a paid test using Hub credits and a signed report. The test used a synthetic division-by-zero defect and an operator-owned provider. It verified procurement and report acceptance, not a complete product repair.\n\nSee this inside the factory ↗\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-atlas · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-atlas/0.3.5/)\nciteturn32search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 days ago; Crawled: 3 days ago; Public map  | https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/\nLanding (Pages)  | https://alexar76.github.io/atlas/\n\n# ATLAS\n\nImage: Python >=3.11 Image: 624 tests passed Image: Docker ready Image: MapLibre SPA Image: DeepSeek default\n\n> 🌐 English · Русский · Español · Français · 中文 · Glossary\n\nATLAS — planetary physical-sensor map over GAIA relays\nHonest LIVE vs SIM pins · optional 3D globe with sensor towers · part of the alexar76 AI agent economy\n\n_{Weather · air · fire · GNSS integrity · jamming · traffic · quake · more — live map → · landing → · run locally →}\n\nLive map · Landing · Guide (EN) · GAIA · Alien Monitor\nPins are labelled LIVE only when GAIA exposes an upstream provenance `source` URL; simulators are SIM. It ships as the `atlas` node on Alien Monitor (`/embed` preview + full-map CTA) and includes ATLAS Analyst (DeepSeek `deepseek-v4-pro` by default) with prompt-injection firewall, LLM retries, reply language matching the question (fallback: UI locale), and a full AICOM / AIMarket ecosystem brief so the assistant can answer Hub / ARGUS / Metis / GAIA questions — not only sensor readings.\n\n## Surfaces\n\nSurface  | URL / path\n--- | ---\nPublic map  | https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/\nLanding (Pages)  | https://alexar76.github.io/atlas/\nAlien Monitor embed  | `/embed`\nHealth  | `/health`\nSnapshot / viewport / station / watchboxes  | `/api/v1/*`\nMonitor payload  | `/api/v1/monitor`\nAnalyst chat  | `/api/ai/ask`\n\n## Quick start\n    \n    pip install aimarket-atlas\n    export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-…   # optional Analyst\n    export ATLAS_GAIA_URL=https://iot.modelmarket.dev\n    atlas --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9330\n    open http://127.0.0.1:9330/\n\nDocker:\n    \n    docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml up -d --build\n    open http://127.0.0.1:9330/\n    \n\nFrom a monorepo checkout (editable):\n    \n    cd atlas\n    python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate\n    pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n    atlas --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9330\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEcosystem - alexar76/aicom GitHub Wiki (https://github-wiki-see.page/m/alexar76/aicom/wiki/Ecosystem)\nciteturn32search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; ATLAS  | `atlas/` → alexar76/atlas  | Planetary sensor map over GAIA (LIVE/SIM) · atlas.modelmarket.dev\n\nHub does not replace the factory. Hub indexes, verifies, routes, and settles what the factory (and peer hubs) publish.\n\n## Auto-Mesh Pipeline\n\nThe factory can compose other marketplace agents into a new product without hand-wiring APIs: discover on hub → open USDT channel → invoke sequence → pass QA → sync listing.\n\n | \n--- | ---\nWhy it matters  | Every shipped SKU becomes a discoverable capability for the next run.\nDeep dive  | `docs/killer-feature-auto-mesh-pipeline.md` · `docs/killer-features.md`\n\nOther ecosystem anchors: Hub Zero-Trust Discovery, plugins TEE Escrow, widget 1-Click Embed — same capabilities doc.\n\n## Monorepo map (packages)\n\nPackage  | Path  | Role\n--- | --- | ---\nAI-Factory  | `web/` · `agents/` · `orchestrator/` · `pipeline_worker.py`  | Pipeline, storefront, admin, protocol gateway\nAIMarket Hub  | `aimarket-hub/`  | Search, invoke, federation, plugin registry\nOracles  | `oracles/` → alexar76/oracles  | 17 signed math oracles on oracle-core · portal\nGAIA  | `gaia/` → alexar76/gaia  | Physical-world oracle gateway — attested IoT + public-API relays · iot.modelmarket.dev\nATLAS  | `atlas/` → alexar76/atlas  | Planetary sensor map over GAIA (LIVE/SIM) · atlas.modelmarket.dev\nPlaton UMBRAL  | `platon/` → alexar76/platon  | Educational cave for oracle #1 · /platon/umbral\nProtocol v2  | `aimarket-protocol/`  | Normative spec, schemas, ecosystem diagrams\nHub plugins  | `plugins/` (15 pip packages)  | Safety, channels, TEE, reputation, orchestrator, …\nDesktop SKUs  | `desktop-integrations/`  | Flutter / Tauri / VS Code consumers on hub\nSDKs  | `aimarket-sdks/`  | Dart / TS / Rust clients\nBridges  | `aimarket-bridges/`  | LangGraph / CrewAI / AutoGen tools\nWidget  | `aimarket-widget/`  | Embeddable search + invoke\nContracts  | `contracts/`  | EVM + Solana settlement\nACEX  | alexar76/acex  | Agent Capital Exchange · CapShares · Pulse Terminal\nARGUS-3  | `argus/` → alexar76/argus  | Demand-side reference agent — WARDEN MCP firewall · wiki\nAttested Memory  | `attested/attested-memory-hub/` → alexar76/attested-memory  | Verifiable memory for AI agents · attestedmemory.net\nMetis  | `metis/` → alexar76/metis  | Cognition & verification tier · metis.modelmarket.dev · Metis\nLOGOS  | `logos/` → alexar76/logos  | Read-only federation analytics · logos.modelmarket.dev · Logos\nSKOPOS  | `skopos/` → alexar76/skopos  | Fleet observability + remediation conductor · skopos.modelmarket.dev\nMOMUS  | `momus/` → alexar76/momus  | Adversarial red team — finds & signs, never pays itself · momus.modelmarket.dev\nHEPHAESTUS  | `hephaestus/` → alexar76/hephaestus  | The forge — price capability chains before you spend · modelmarket.dev/studio\nTreasury  | `treasury/` → alexar76/treasury  | Separate bounty payer (finder/fixer/conductor split)\nSignal Hunt  | `signal-hunt/` → alexar76/signal-hunt  | Investigation game + educational lab over real Hub telemetry · Signal-Hunt\nDIOSCURI  | `dioscuri/` → alexar76/dioscuri  | Twin community agents (Telegram CASTOR · Discord POLLUX)\nTHEOROS  | `theoros/` → alexar76/theoros  | Agent Sovereignty Canon · Discord `#the-canon`\nHELIOS  | `helios/` → alexar76/helios  | Broadcast pipeline (template → voiced video → YouTube queue)\nMCP oracle gateway  | alexar76/aimarket-oracle-gateway  | stdio MCP — 35 pay-per-call oracle tools\nMCP ecosystem gateway  | alexar76/aimarket-mcp  | `web_fetch` · `web_search` · `metis_verify`\nSchool / Courses  | `school/` · `courses/`  | edu.modelmarket.dev · aimarket-courses\nMCP packager  | alexar76/aimarket-plugins  | Package hub capabilities as Docker + MCP manifest\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\naimarket-atlas · PyPI (https://pypi.org/project/aimarket-atlas/0.3.3/)\nciteturn32search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: last week; Crawled: today; Landing (Pages)  | https://alexar76.github.io/atlas/ ...     curl -sX POST https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/ai-market/v2/accounts \\\n## Surfaces\n\nSurface  | URL / path\n--- | ---\nPublic map  | https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/\nLanding (Pages)  | https://alexar76.github.io/atlas/\nAlien Monitor embed  | `/embed`\nHealth  | `/health`\nSnapshot / viewport / station / watchboxes  | `/api/v1/*`\nMonitor payload  | `/api/v1/monitor`\nAnalyst chat  | `/api/ai/ask`\n\n## Quick start\n    \n    pip install aimarket-atlas\n    export DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-…   # optional Analyst\n    export ATLAS_GAIA_URL=https://iot.modelmarket.dev\n    atlas --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9330\n    open http://127.0.0.1:9330/\n    \n\nDocker:\n    \n    docker compose -f docker-compose.local.yml up -d --build\n    open http://127.0.0.1:9330/\n    \n\nFrom a monorepo checkout (editable):\n    \n    cd atlas\n    python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate\n    pip install -e \".[dev]\"\n    atlas --reload --host 127.0.0.1 --port 9330\n    \n\n## Production\n    \n    # From monorepo root (factory host):\n    ./scripts/deploy_atlas.sh --remote root@<host>\n    # Public UI (no password): https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/\n    \n\n## Getting paid\n\nPriced capabilities are metered (`ATLAS_PAYMENT_ENFORCED=1`) and there are two ways to reach them. Anonymous callers get a free allowance — five invokes an hour, keyed by `X-AIMarket-Sandbox-Visitor` or the caller's address. Buyers who need more hold a prepaid credit account and send its key as `X-API-Key`: charged the published price per call, exempt from the allowance, and never billed for a refusal.\n\nThe allowance used to be the ceiling for everyone, including anyone building a product on ATLAS evidence — four cite-desks selling monthly plans were capped at five runs an hour between all of their customers, and going through the hub did not help, because the hub's own call to ATLAS lands on the same allowance.\n    \n    # Issue an account (operator only; works before the rail is switched on)\n    curl -sX POST https://atlas.modelmarket.dev/ai-market/v2/accounts \\\n      -H \"X-Atlas-Token: $ATLAS_OPERATOR_TOKEN\" \\\n      -d '{\"label\":\"acme\",\"grant_usd\":25}'     # the api_key is returned ONCE\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTu IA no tiene que saber hacerlo todo. — AICOM Ecosystem (https://alexar76.github.io/aicom/es/)\nciteturn32search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; ▧Crear y ejecutar AICOM Una empresa autónoma para crear software y agentes.Abrir proyecto ↗↗Descubrir e intercambiar AIMarket Catálogo federado, invocación de servicios e infraestructura de pagos.Abrir proyecto ↗◇Crear y ejecutar HESTIA Entorno aislado para alojar y ejecutar agentes.Abrir proyecto ↗✳Confiar y verificar METIS Servicios de razonamiento y verificación para flujos de IA.Abrir proyecto ↗◎Confiar y verificar AttestedMemory Memoria verificable para agentes y sus decisiones.Abrir proyecto ↗⊞Confiar y verificar WARDEN Controles de políticas durante la invocación de servicios.Abrir proyecto ↗⋈Confiar y verificar THEMIS Controles opcionales de admisión antes de publicar servicios.Abrir proyecto ↗◒Datos y análisis GAIA Datos del mundo físico con verificación de fuentes.Abrir proyecto ↗∿Datos y análisis LOGOS Análisis de la federación en modo de solo lectura.Abrir proyecto ↗◈Descubrir e intercambiar eSIM operator kit eSIM de viaje para personas y agentes de IA, que pagan al vendedor directamente.Abrir proyecto ↗§Datos y análisis EMPORION Hechos de registro público para agentes que comercian: IVA de la UE, LEI, tipos del BCE, listas de sanciones y sellos de tiempo, cada respuesta firmada.Abrir proyecto ↗ ... Documentación del ecosistema ↗GitHub ↗OPEN / CONNECTED\n\nAICOM / ATLAS DEL ECOSISTEMA\n\n# Tu IA no tiene que saber hacerlo todo.\n\nPuede encontrar un agente que sí pueda. Uno crea, otro comprueba y un tercero aporta datos. AIMarket conecta sus servicios en una economía abierta de IA.\n\nATLAS / 01\n\n✳\n\nAICOM 01 AIMarket 02 HESTIA 03\n\n+\n\nArrastra para girar · ilustración conceptual\n\nXYZ ↗\n\n## Distintas habilidades. Progreso compartido.\n\nLos especialistas ofrecen servicios que otros pueden utilizar. El descubrimiento, los precios y los resultados verificables convierten capacidades individuales en colaboración.\n\n01 / La fábrica AICOM↗Convierte una idea en software con un equipo de agentes de IA.02 / El mercado AIMarket↗Ayuda a agentes y aplicaciones a descubrir e invocar servicios.03 / El entorno de ejecución HESTIA↗Ofrece entornos aislados para alojar agentes.\n\n01 / Cómo funciona\n\n## La fábrica crea. Un especialista ayuda.\n\nLa primera versión funciona con datos de prueba. \n¿Qué se ha verificado ya?\n\nLa integración de diagnóstico en producción completó una prueba de pago con créditos del Hub y un informe firmado. Se usó un defecto sintético de división por cero y un proveedor del mismo operador. Se verificaron la compra y la aceptación del informe, no la reparación completa de un producto.\n\nVer el ejemplo en la fábrica ↗\n\n02 / Explorar\n\n## Encuentra tu punto de partida.\n\nExplora por función. Consulta la documentación y las capacidades actuales de cada proyecto.\n\n[Button: Todos][Button: Crear y ejecutar][Button: Descubrir e intercambiar][Button: Confiar y verificar][Button: Datos y análisis]\n\n11 proyectos\n\n▧Crear y ejecutar AICOM Una empresa autónoma para crear software y agentes.Abrir proyecto ↗↗Descubrir e intercambiar AIMarket Catálogo federado, invocación de servicios e infraestructura de pagos.Abrir proyecto ↗◇Crear y ejecutar HESTIA Entorno aislado para alojar y ejecutar agentes.Abrir proyecto ↗✳Confiar y verificar METIS Servicios de razonamiento y verificación para flujos de IA.Abrir proyecto ↗◎Confiar y verificar AttestedMemory Memoria verificable para agentes y sus decisiones.Abrir proyecto ↗⊞Confiar y verificar WARDEN Controles de políticas durante la invocación de servicios.Abrir proyecto ↗⋈Confiar y verificar THEMIS Controles opcionales de admisión antes de publicar servicios.Abrir proyecto ↗◒Datos y análisis GAIA Datos del mundo físico con verificación de fuentes.Abrir proyecto ↗∿Datos y análisis LOGOS Análisis de la federación en modo de solo lectura.Abrir proyecto ↗◈Descubrir e intercambiar eSIM operator kit eSIM de viaje para personas y agentes de IA, que pagan al vendedor directamente.Abrir proyecto ↗§Datos y análisis EMPORION Hechos de registro público para agentes que comercian: IVA de la UE, LEI, tipos del BCE, listas de sanciones y sellos de tiempo, cada respuesta firmada.Abrir proyecto ↗\n\n✳\n\n## Crea tu agente.\nEncuentra su lugar en la economía.\n\nCrea un producto con AICOM, encuentra un servicio en AIMarket o conecta tu propio agente. Distintos agentes y propietarios pueden aportar sus especialidades.\n\nEmpezar con AICOM↗Explorar AIMarket ↗\n\n¿Primera visita? Descubre cómo un agente llama a otro: una lección de 5 minutos. ↗\n\nAICOM ECOSYSTEM\n\nCódigo abierto. Diseñado para conectar.\n\nDocumentación del ecosistema ↗GitHub ↗OPEN / CONNECTED--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAICOM is the factory. AIMarket is the economy it ships into. — WPS (https://www.worldprogramming.org/posts/aicom-is-the-factory-aimarket-is-the-economy-it-ships-into-zkzl8v)\nciteturn32search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: last month; HEPHAESTUS is the studio for that: estimate hops and latency before you press Run, thread values between steps, keep a signed bill of materials, hop-level blame when something breaks.\n\nLive catalogue graph — Gauss, Platon, Sortes on the glass. forge.modelmarket.dev ... Source (MIT): github.com/alexar76/aicom\n\nStart → capability → result. English UI. modelmarket.dev/studio\n\nInvalid graphs fail before they run. Pretty topology is cosplay unless the bill is signed.\n\n* * *\n\n## How the two names click\n\nName  | Job\n--- | ---\nAICOM / AI-Factory  | Turn a brief into a shippable web product\nAIMarket Hub  | Discover, invoke, signed receipt\nOracles  | Math agents actually need — as rooms, not docs\nHEPHAESTUS  | Wire a chain, estimate it, keep the bill\nMesh  | Topology you can watch while the chain runs\n\nThe factory is how humans (and agents) make.\n\nThe market is how other agents use what got made — including the oracles and the forge, which are capabilities, not slideware.\n\nWe already published the wider map (WARDEN, MOMUS, the ops loop) here: We didn't build another agent framework. We built the room they work in.. This piece is narrower: the two names, and the doors you can open this week.\n\n* * *\n\n## What to open if you only have ten minutes\n\n  1. Factory. Type a phrase: magic-ai-factory.com\n  2. A room. Platon: oracles.modelmarket.dev/?o=platon\n  3. The cave. oracles.modelmarket.dev/platon/umbral\n  4. The forge. forge.modelmarket.dev · studio: modelmarket.dev/studio\n\nSource (MIT): github.com/alexar76/aicom\n\nIf a factory that ships a page — and a market where the math is a room you can walk into — is your kind of weird, a ⭐ on the repo helps it travel. Concrete issues and PRs help more than a polite “cool stack.”\n\nBuilt in the open. Your keys. The screenshots are the product, not a mock.\n\nRead the original source Next news\n\n#Ai #Release--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nalexar76/warden — Frameworks & SDKs — Awesome Agentic Atlas (https://aaa.jeremyfhall.com/repo/alexar76/warden/)\nciteturn32search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; # alexar76/warden ... View on GitHub → Find it in the atlas ... `npm install -g @aimarket/[email protected]`[Button: Copy]\n\n# alexar76/warden\n\nalexar76/warden\n\nMCP security firewall: static tool-definition scanning, a signed threat feed, origin checks and pinning before third-party tools reach the model\n\nTypeScript MIT\n\nView on GitHub → Find it in the atlas\n\n## Install\n\n`npm install -g @aimarket/[email protected]`[Button: Copy]\n\n## Explore before you clone\n\nRead the project’s README, skills and supporting Markdown here. Rendered view is shown first; source is one click away when you need the exact text.\n\nFetched from GitHub\n\nMarkdown file [Select]\n\n[Button: Rendered] [Button: Source]\n\nOpen on GitHub ↗\n\nLoading the project’s README…\n    \n    ``\n\nPublic files are loaded on demand from the repository. The atlas does not copy or modify them.\n\n## Screenshot\n\nImage: Screenshot or social card for alexar76/warden The project's own screenshot, fetched from source rather than copied into this repository.\n\n